  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The similar names in several languages may reflect the spread of the crop. Jeremiah places the noun šāqēd beside the verb šōqēd ‘watching’. The wordplay is explicit, while their historical relationship remains uncertain.\n\nJob.21.32 also uses the verb at a burial mound. The identity of the one keeping watch there is uncertain.\n\nMerged from `shaqed`, `shaqad` on 2026-11-20: one root, one entry."
